  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "like + noun: affirmative (I like football); distinguish noun objects from -ing activity forms",
      "title_form": "Me gusta + sustantivo",
      "title_target": "I like + noun",
      "description_md_form": "Para decir que algo te gusta, usa **I like** + un **sustantivo**. Por ejemplo: *I like football* (Me gusta el fútbol).\n\n**Importante:** en inglés, las actividades se expresan con la forma **-ing** del verbo, que funciona como un sustantivo. Por ejemplo: *I like swimming* (Me gusta nadar).\n\n**Diferencia clave:**\n- **Sustantivo** (cosa): *I like music* → Me gusta la música.\n- **Actividad** (-ing): *I like singing* → Me gusta cantar.\n\nUsa **I like** para hablar de tus pasatiempos y tiempo libre.",
      "description_md_target": "To say you like something, use **I like** + a **noun**. For example: *I like football*.\n\n**Important:** in English, activities use the **-ing** form of the verb, which works as a noun. For example: *I like swimming*.\n\n**Key difference:**\n- **Noun** (thing): *I like music*.\n- **Activity** (-ing): *I like singing*.\n\nUse **I like** to talk about your hobbies and free time.",
      "grammar_structure": "I like + noun / I like + verb-ing",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "like_affirmative",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "like",
            "I like football."
          ],
          [
            "You",
            "like",
            "You like tennis."
          ],
          [
            "He/She/It",
            "likes",
            "He likes music."
          ],
          [
            "We",
            "like",
            "We like games."
          ],
          [
            "They",
            "like",
            "They like films."
          ]
        ]
      },
